# P0 / P1 / P2 pretrainings of normal_C: model B without the row steps (encoder col_v0_normal, depth 6)
# (rriva, 2026-11-26).  The model is the base config: CONFIG=saint_normal_C.
# Same recipe for every model of this experiment:
#   40 epochs, batch 12800, AdamW lr 1e-3, gradient clip 1.0 (arm=pretrain), contrastive T 0.1, noise lambda 0.4,
#   no dropout; WSD: warmup 2 epochs, constant, decay over epochs 32-40; no early stopping, downstream loads last.ckpt.
#   p0 = per-object contrastive on the track and jet-feature embeddings (the aggregator is not trained)
#   p1 = p0 + jet contrastive (weight 1.0, T 0.1) on the aggregator output
#   p2 = jet contrastive only (per-object contrastive weight 0)
# Seeds 42 424 4242 42424 (owner, 2026-11-26), two runs per card (SLOTS_PER_GPU=2).
# @mem below: the CPU estimate used at launch (experiments/dev/2026-11-26_cpu-mem-estimate); see CORRECTED.
# @est: seconds per epoch WHILE two share a card, upper bound = 2 x normal_RC's P1 alone on an A40 (6650 s);
#       40 epochs = 148 h of the 167.5 h a 7-day job leaves.
# Launched 2026-11-26 (stage P_normal_C_20261126_123145):
#   CONFIG=saint_normal_C MAX_EPOCHS=40 SEEDS="42 424 4242 42424" WALLTIME=7-00:00:00 EST_SECONDS_PER_EPOCH=13300 \
#   GPU_NODE=gpu-L40S-open,gpu-A40 STAGE=P_normal_C PACKS=2 SLOTS_PER_GPU=2 GPU_BUDGET_GIB=40 MEM_PER_GPU_GB=48 \
#   CELLS=experiments/2026-11_pretrain-saint-small/configs/P_normal_C.cells bash slurm/ssl_pack.sh
#   (normal_C: 2 packs on 2026-11-26, the third when a job slot frees:
#    STAGE_DIR=<repo>/experiments/2026-11_pretrain-saint-small/outputs/P_normal_C_20261126_123145 PACKS=1 bash slurm/ssl_pack.sh)
# CORRECTED 2026-11-26 23:15 in the stage (not yet started): the CPU estimate was 1.5-1.9x too low for small_RC, so
# normal_C runs ONE per card first: @mem = 40 (the only safe bound is normal_RC's own peak, up to 42.5 GiB at batch
# 12800) and @est = 6650 s (normal_RC's P1 alone on an A40; normal_C does a subset of its work), so each card runs two
# normal_C one after the other.  Later claims can be paired once the first epoch has measured the real peak.
p0_normal_C  arm=pretrain chunk_size=512 datamodule.batch_size=12800 optimizer.lr=1e-3 optimizer.schedule=wsd optimizer.warmup_epochs=2 optimizer.decay_frac=0.2 ~callbacks.early_stopping @est=13300 @mem=9
p1_normal_C  arm=pretrain chunk_size=512 datamodule.batch_size=12800 optimizer.lr=1e-3 optimizer.schedule=wsd optimizer.warmup_epochs=2 optimizer.decay_frac=0.2 ~callbacks.early_stopping pretrain.loss_weights.jet_contrastive=1.0 @est=13300 @mem=20
p2_normal_C  arm=pretrain chunk_size=512 datamodule.batch_size=12800 optimizer.lr=1e-3 optimizer.schedule=wsd optimizer.warmup_epochs=2 optimizer.decay_frac=0.2 ~callbacks.early_stopping pretrain.loss_weights.contrastive=0.0 pretrain.loss_weights.jet_contrastive=1.0 @est=13300 @mem=16
